From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruiyangke <me@ry.ke>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gpui_windows: Drop a closed window's late reports

Hiding or destroying a window makes Windows report deactivation and, under
the cursor, mouse leave after GPUI has already removed the window, and each
report then logs "window not found". Take the active-status and hover
callbacks on drop, as the visibility callback already is.

Remove when upstream gpui_windows drops them on close.
---
 crates/gpui_windows/src/window.rs | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/gpui_windows/src/window.rs b/crates/gpui_windows/src/window.rs
index 95e45116..a0b7819d 100644
--- a/crates/gpui_windows/src/window.rs
+++ b/crates/gpui_windows/src/window.rs
@@ -851,6 +851,12 @@ impl Drop for WindowsWindow {
         // `DestroyWindow` below sends `WM_SHOWWINDOW`; without a callback the
         // resulting visibility report has nothing to notify.
         self.0.state.callbacks.visibility_change.take();
+        // Hiding or destroying an active window deactivates it after GPUI has
+        // already removed it, and the report would find no window.
+        self.0.state.callbacks.active_status_change.take();
+        // Hiding a window under the cursor sends `WM_MOUSELEAVE`, which would
+        // report on a window GPUI has already removed.
+        self.0.state.callbacks.hovered_status_change.take();
         // clone this `Rc` to prevent early release of the pointer
         let this = self.0.clone();
         self.0
